--- body ---
## Context
X2 lost an hour to a schema break nobody had noticed: upstream renamed the
index tables, so `passages` — once the FTS5 virtual table — is now a plain
table with `passages_fts` beside it. Every pre-existing index on the author's
machine became unreadable, and the runbook step that used one could not run.

The sweep asked whether anything else in `bench/` carries the same
assumption. Two drivers do, and both open a REAL index rather than building
their own:

- **`bench/index_concentration.mjs:138`** — `CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE ... USING
  fts5vocab(passages, row)`. Confirmed against the rebuilt 477 512-passage
  index: `Error: stepping, no such fts5 table: temp.passages`. So this driver
  cannot run against any index built by v1.9.0.
- **`bench/bm25_idf_effect.mjs:4`** — opens the hardcoded path
  `/home/haduong/.zoteus-bench-0003/search-index.sqlite` and queries the old
  shape. Two defects in one line: the pre-rename schema, and a hardcoded path
  where the house rule requires a CLI parameter.

Checked and NOT affected, recorded so the next sweep does not re-derive it:
`constrained_match.mjs` already uses `passages_fts`; `fts5_bench.mjs` and
`cosine_fusion.mjs` build their own tables and are self-consistent —
`cosine_fusion.mjs` is in fact already new-schema-shaped.

Why this clears the severity floor: it bites the science. STATE.md quotes
0013's concentration figures, and they were produced by a driver that can no
longer run against a current index — so those numbers cannot be re-measured
or refuted, only believed.

## Relevant files
- `bench/index_concentration.mjs` — `fts5vocab(passages, row)` at line 138
- `bench/bm25_idf_effect.mjs` — hardcoded path and old schema at line 4
- `bench/results/0013-concentration/` — the artifacts whose driver is broken
- A current-schema index exists at
  `/home/haduong/data/projets/zoteus-bench/x2-rebuild/` (477 512 passages),
  built for X2, so neither repair needs a fresh 264 s build

## Actions
1. Point `index_concentration.mjs` at `passages_fts`, and have it FAIL LOUDLY
   with the schema it found when the expected table is absent — a driver that
   silently measures the wrong table is the defect class this ticket exists
   for.
2. Give `bm25_idf_effect.mjs` a `--db` argument with no default, per the
   no-hardcoded-paths rule, and move it to the new schema.
3. Re-run both against `x2-rebuild/` and compare with the committed 0013
   artifacts. A changed number is a finding, not a nuisance: say which of the
   two runs is right and why, in the artifact.

## Test
The repair is verified by running, not by reading — the old code errors on a
current index, which is the red step. Assert on the error path too: point the
repaired driver at a pre-rename index and confirm it names the schema it
found rather than returning zero.

## Verification
- [ ] both drivers run against `x2-rebuild/` and emit their artifacts
- [ ] both refuse loudly on a pre-rename index, naming the schema
- [ ] `bm25_idf_effect.mjs` has no hardcoded path
- [ ] 0013's figures re-measured, and any change explained in the artifact
      and propagated to STATE.md through the figure guard

## Invariants
- `make check` stays green; the figure guard reports 0 stale.
- No committed artifact is edited to match a new run without the artifact
  saying which run produced it.

## Exit criteria
- Both drivers run against a current-schema index, refuse loudly against an
  old one, and 0013's quoted figures are either confirmed or corrected with
  the reason recorded.
